--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -3,3 +3,19 @@
 A small TypeScript library, with no runtime dependency, of building blocks for our services that store,
 exchange and update JSON: configuration files, API payloads and stored records. It is imported by the
 other projects of the team, so its behaviour must follow the published standards it implements.
+
+## JSON Pointer
+
+`resolvePointer(document, pointer)` (exported from `src/index.ts`) returns the value of a JSON document
+that a [JSON Pointer (RFC 6901)](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6901) refers to. The empty pointer
+`""` refers to the whole document.
+
+```ts
+resolvePointer({ foo: ["bar", "baz"] }, "/foo/1"); // "baz"
+```
+
+It throws when the pointer is not valid (no leading `/`, or a `~` not followed by `0` or `1`) or when it
+does not resolve: missing member, out-of-range or non-canonical array index (`01`), the `-` token (which
+names a nonexistent element), or a step into a primitive. Only own members of objects are followed.
+
+Run the tests with `npm test` (Node 22.18+, which runs the TypeScript sources directly).
